## CQ-HOP-02 | rug crack overlay stays on the block; the rug still draws its fringe
@group client
@commands survival; place a straw rug, a hay rug and a canvas rug on grass, and a stone block; mine each slowly (no efficiency) and watch the crack, then look at each placed rug from the side
@pass the crack shows only within the block's 0 to 1 box on all three rugs, nothing on the fringe that hangs past the edge; the rugs still draw their fringe when not being mined; the stone's crack is unchanged; no `BreakOverlayClipMixin` error in latest.log
@fails `BreakOverlayClipMixin` not applied (Forge `BlockRenderDispatcher.renderBreakingTexture` signature), `client/BreakOverlayClip` quad filter, block tag missing (SQ-HOP-14)
@draft visual mid-break: the crack draws only while attack is held, and the driver releases held keys at the end of a walk step before any capture; needs a capture inside a held walk (driver feature) or the owner watching the three rugs

